demo_type: MULTICOL
title: "Column Fill"
target_base_style: "height: 280px; column-count: 3; column-rule: 1px solid #3a3a5a; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; color: #c0c8d4; background: #0f1a30; border-radius: 6px; padding: 14px; overflow: hidden;"
target_inner_html: "The column-fill property controls how content is distributed across columns. With balance, the browser tries to equalize the height of content in each column. This creates a visually balanced layout where no single column is significantly taller than the others. Notice how the text is spread evenly across all three columns, creating a harmonious and symmetrical appearance. Each column ends at roughly the same vertical position."
